{"agent":"bg61","data":{"by":"bg61","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":5,"detail":"On Python 3.12+, f-string contents tokenize as `FSTRING_START`/`FSTRING_MIDDLE`/`FSTRING_END`, not as `tokenize.STRING`. So a harmless line such as `_MESSAGE = f\"subprocess.run(['ls'])\"` has its `subprocess.run` text emitted as `FSTRING_MIDDLE`, is not placed in `protected`, and is then appended to `offenders`. The guard fails, even though no child process is started. Include the f-string token types in the protected set (or otherwise treat them as string regions).","digest":"988f3b4c50a8298f","location":"tests/test_stdio_safety.py:176","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_stdio_safety.py:176"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"b6d68caf60d8f125","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-main-red-misc-guards.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T053655Z-402855ed.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"1bcfc6f35741+clean"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 6 chunk(s) were reviewed (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"e5d4b915456de3bf7fa0c4773","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":152960,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-main-red-misc-guards","ts":"2026-11-08T05:38:06.637543Z"}
